nd the horizontal.  2. The second diagram in the top right also depicts a square with a diagonal line from corner A to C, with multiple force vectors labeled mg pointing downwards along t\he line, representing gravitational force acting on the mass m.  3. The third diagram in the bottom left shows a similar setup with additional vectors representing velocity components along the diagonal, specifically indicating changes in velocity due to \angular motion.  4. The fourth diagram in the bottom right simplifies the representation focusing on rotational motion with vectors indicating rotational velocity and its components, and a note stating that the angle f equals /2.  Each diagram includes co\ordinate axes labeled x and y, enhancing the understanding of the vector components and their directions.␀)/K 2/P 21924 0 R/Pg 951 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj22113 0 obj<</K 3/P 21924 0 R/Pg 951 0 R/S/Caption/Type/StructElem>>endobj22114 0 obj<</K[4 22214 0 R 6]/P 21924 0 R/Pg 951 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj22115 0 obj<</K 7/P 21924 0 R/Pg 951 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj22116 0 obj<</K[8 22199 0 R 10 22200 0 R 13 22201 0 R 16 22202 0 R 19 22203 0 R 22 22204 0 R 25 22205 0 R 28 22206 0 R 31 22207 0 R 34 22208 0 R 37 22209 0 R 40 22210 0 R 43 22211 0 R 46 22212 0 R 49]/P 21924 0 R/Pg 951 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj22117 0 obj<</K[50 22192 0 R 53 22193 0 R 56 22194 0 R 59 22195 0 R 61 22196 0 R 64 22197 0 R 67]/P 21924 0 R/Pg 951 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj22118 0 obj<</K[1 22185 0 R 4 22186 0 R 7 22187 0 R 10 22188 0 R 12 22189 0 R 15 22190 0 R 18]/P 21924 0 R/Pg 954 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj22119 0 obj<</ActualText(\\bALT{}\\label{cons.quantita.moto.esempio1} R_x\\ap{ext}=0 \\quad \\Rightarrow\\quad Q_x=\\text{const.} \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad Q_x^0=Q_x^f\\,.\\eALT{} )/Border[0 0 0]/K 19/P 21924 0 R/Pg 954 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj22120 0 obj<</K 22/P 21924 0 R/Pg 954 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj22121 0 obj<</K