onnected to the center O by a radius R. An angle \(t\) is shown between the radius \and the x-axis. A vector v, labeled as R, is depicted perpendicular to the radius at point P\(t\), indicating the velocity vector of P\(t\) as it moves along the circle's path. On the right:Diagram illustrating circular motion with a focus on acceleration\ components. The image shows a circle centered at point O with radius R, marked on the x-axis. A point P\(t\) on the circumference represents a position at time t. Two vectors originate from P\(t\): \\\(a_t = R\\dot{\\theta}\\\) indicating tangential acce\leration, and \\\(a_n = R\\dot{\\theta}^2\\\) pointing towards the center, representing normal acceleration. The coordinate axes x and y are labeled, with y pointing upwards and x extending to the right.␀)/K 50/P 29982 0 R/Pg 199 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj30009 0 obj<</K 51/P 29982 0 R/Pg 199 0 R/S/Caption/Type/StructElem>>endobj30010 0 obj<</K[2 31890 0 R 5 31891 0 R 8 31892 0 R 10 31893 0 R 12]/P 29982 0 R/Pg 202 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj30011 0 obj<</ActualText(\\bUnALT{} \\vv=R{\\dot \\theta }\\tt \\qquad \\aa=R\\ddot{\\theta}\\tt+R\\dot{\\theta}^2\\nn\\,.\\eUnALT{} )/Border[0 0 0]/K 13/P 29982 0 R/Pg 202 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj30012 0 obj<</K[15 31887 0 R 18 31888 0 R 21 31889 0 R 24]/P 29982 0 R/Pg 202 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj30013 0 obj<</K[25 31886 0 R 28]/P 29982 0 R/Pg 202 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj30014 0 obj<</K[29 31883 0 R 32 31884 0 R 35 31885 0 R 38]/P 29982 0 R/Pg 202 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj30015 0 obj<</ActualText(\\bUnALT{} P\(q\) \\qquad \\vv_P=\\pder{P}{q}{\\dot{q}}\\eUnALT{} )/Border[0 0 0]/K 39/P 29982 0 R/Pg 202 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj30016 0 obj<</K[41 31878 0 R 43 31879 0 R 45 31880 0 R 48]/P 29982 0 R/Pg 202 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj30017 0 obj<</K 50/P 29982 0 R/Pg 202 0 R/S/H3/Type/StructElem>>endobj30018 0 obj<</K[51 31876 0 R 53]/P 29982 0 R/Pg 202 0 R/S/P/Type/